Aaron Sampson here with a starter guide  for the titanfall beta with the close  titanfall beta set to run from Friday  February 14th to Wednesday February 19th  some of you will most certainly find  yourself in the chest area of one of  these walking monstrosity if you care to  be the thing that punches the squishy  things on the ground and not the squishy  thing that gets punched then you should  pay attention for starters there are  three modes in the build of titanfall  that we previewed attrition which is  team deathmatch hardpoint domination  which is conquest and last Titan  standing which is destroy the mechanical  things to win both attrition and  hardpoint domination will see you  leaping out of a dropship and saddled  with a four minute countdown timer until  you get your Titan you can shorten this  time by killing creep other pilots and  later on by rodeoing enemy titans holy  crap look how fast that rodeo bleeds the  countdown timer when that timer does run  down you may call in one of three  classes of Titans the Atlas which is the  one most likely to be in the beta comes  in assault tank in artillery  specializations so which one do you want  to be in that depends on what map you're  playing the assault and artillery  variants of the Atlas are great for  close quarters urban warfare on Angel  City  the artillery variant puts out immense  damage at close range with circular  volleys of Rocky's these rockets travel  too slowly to have an effect on longer  sightlines so contrary to what our  Tillery does in real life think of this  class as a close quarters bruiser the  assault variant is also good on Angel  City and as an all-around fighter  utilizing the EXO 16 chain gun the chain  guns rate of fire also makes it one of  the more effective weapons against  dismounted pilots the titan also comes  with an auto eject feature which means  you won't end up like this guy  as a bonus the auto reject also chips  your pilots cloak power to see you  safely away or just land on the Titan  that killed you and Rodeo it to death  now let's talk about the tank variant of  the Atlas this beauty sports a 40  millimeter cannon that works like a DMR  for this reason you should take the tank  out for a spin on the fracture map the  tank also comes stock with a nuclear  ejection feature which is amazing here's  how it works if you find yourself  outnumbered and getting gang beat by  enemy Titans lure them closer now closer  even closer now flip the bird is you  eject and watch them explode as your  Titan self destructs haha you live all  three variants also come with the bullet  catchy vortex shield which vacuums up  incoming fire and returns it to its  owner be careful with the return part  lest you end up playing past the bombs  with an enemy Titan and then running out  of catch juice also if you see an enemy  Titan deploy the vortex shield  I'd recommend holding your fire there's  nothing more satisfying than shooting an  enemy Titan making it mad catching its  bullets and then throwing them back in  its face starting at level 10 you'll  unlock custom slots and can get your big  metal paws on slave warheads that  replace rocket salvo and also electric  smoke that replaces vortex shield  Electric smoke releases a burning cloud  into the air and is great for frying  enemy pilots who are busy pulling out  your neck gizzards damaging an enemy  Titan during a fist fight or for  entering a capture point and then  denying access to it for dismounts now  let's talk about titan combat a fight  between two titans is about managing  distance not forgetting to use cover  like you would as a pilot paying  attention to shields in the same way you  wouldn't say halo and knowing when to go  in and rip out a Titans pilots beating  heart make sure you know when to engage  and when to run away because Titans can  be killed fairly easily for more  advanced tactics calling a Titan fall on  an enemy Titan and watch it be crushed  like an actor on sharknado if you see a  friendly Titan about to lose drop your  Titan in front of it has a Titan lands  it deploys a large temporary shield that  can act as cover for your team later  level unlocks  increase the amount of time that shield  is deployed speaking of now that your  Titan is on the ground but far away from  you  set the Titan to follow you or garden  area it won't be as effective at combat  as when you're in it but there's a  couple scenarios where they'll give you  an advantage in hardpoint domination  matches usually one of the capture  points can be reached by titans directly  but not so much for the others leaving  your Titan to guard the outside while  you capture from within is a must  it'll even drop you off on the second  story thanks Titan you will also have to  ditch your Titan when you're getting  rodeoed by enemy pilots the only way to  kill them is to get out and do it  manually do not set your Titan to patrol  when you get out it'll only make the  enemy pilot into a moving target  if the enemy pilot is smarting gets off  to fight you then tell your Titan to  join the fray and light that pile it up  if you died don't worry you're tight and  will fight on in your honour the last  reason to ditch your Titan is to create  a diversion in the epilogue portion of  matches the epilogue is the part at the  end of a match where the winning team  has to chase the losing team to a  dropship everyone has one life and the  objective for the losing team is to get  out alive the dropship can be destroyed  by direct damage so protective as long  as possible  holding out as long as you can in your  Titan and then leaving it to fend for  itself could buy you a few precious  seconds that make you the only person  off the planet large point bonuses are  awarded for teams who can get all their  players spirited away safely but good  luck with that as a matter of fact keep  an eye on the match score if you're  about to lose get to the dropship pickup  point before the epilogue kicks in  there's so much more to talk about in  titanfall hell we didn't even get into  pilots while jumping across the math  donkey kicking players in midair all of  these more shall be yours soon so stay  tuned to game spot for more titanfall  coverage  you
 

